cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ResGate: search-free, reference-free rank-1 abliteration with sep(l) per-layer weighting"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it together with the two works it is
  built on: Arditi et al. 2024 (the foundational method) and Heretic (the
  orthogonalisation step and the rank-1 PRE row-normalised update rule). See
  ATTRIBUTION.md for exactly which parts are whose.
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/kncshw/resgate"
url: "https://github.com/kncshw/resgate"
authors:
  - name: "resgate contributors"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-15"
keywords:
  - abliteration
  - refusal direction
  - mechanistic interpretability
  - AI safety research
  - red teaming
abstract: >-
  A four-step abliteration pipeline totalling 263 lines of core code. It derives
  its target tensor set from a checkpoint's safetensors headers with no
  architecture knowledge, fits a per-layer refusal direction from five prompts
  (one harmful, four harmless) with no reference model and no held-out split,
  weights each layer by sep(l) = ||h_l - abar_l|| / mean_i||g_i,l - abar_l||
  normalised to mean 1, and applies one rank-1 PRE row-normalised weight edit at
  a single global dose K. No search, no Optuna loop, no gradient. Validated on
  dense (Llama-3.1-8B, 64 targets) and MoE (Qwen3.6-35B-A3B 120 targets;
  Gemma-4-26B-A4B 90 targets) checkpoints. Ships a three-way
  REFUSED/DEFLECTED/COMPLIED evaluation, because a keyword refusal count cannot
  distinguish a model that declines from a model that agrees and then says
  nothing.
references:
  - type: conference-paper
    title: "Refusal in Language Models Is Mediated by a Single Direction"
    collection-title: "Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems"
    volume: 37
    year: 2024
    identifiers:
      - type: other
        value: "arXiv:2406.11717"
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.11717"
    authors:
      - family-names: Arditi
        given-names: Andy
      - family-names: Obeso
        given-names: Oscar
      - family-names: Syed
        given-names: Aaquib
      - family-names: Paleka
        given-names: Daniel
      - family-names: Panickssery
        given-names: Nina
      - family-names: Gurnee
        given-names: Wes
      - family-names: Nanda
        given-names: Neel
    notes: >-
      The foundational method: difference-of-means refusal direction plus a
      rank-1 weight edit.
  - type: software
    title: "Heretic"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/p-e-w/heretic"
    license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
    authors:
      - family-names: Weidmann
        given-names: "Philipp Emanuel"
      - name: "Heretic contributors"
    notes: >-
      Source of orthogonalize_direction (main.py:459-469 at the revision this
      method was built against) and of the rank-1 PRE row-normalised update
      rule, verified by reproducing Heretic's published weights to cos 0.99985.
      Also the source of the KeywordRate and KLDivergence metrics reproduced in
      eval/. Heretic is AGPL-3.0-or-later; this repo is licensed
      AGPL-3.0-or-later to match. See the licensing section of ATTRIBUTION.md.
